      "content": "$$\\frac{1}{2}(1 - \\sin x) = -2 \\int_{\\pi/2}^{x} u(\\theta) \\sin \\theta \\cos^{-1} (\\cot \\theta \\tan x) \\, d\\theta.$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 76,
      "topLeftY": 364,
      "bottomRightX": 436,
      "bottomRightY": 382,
      "content": "Now, differentiating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
